    AME 547 - Keyboard Assembly Cell Simulation
    Component: Aluminum Switch Plate (75% Layout, 84-key)

    Reference: Keychron K2 V3
    Material: Aluminum (6061-T6)

    STL verified dimensions (from Blender/FreeCAD export):
      Length (X) : 304.8mm
      Width  (Y) : 114.3mm
      Thickness  : 1.5mm
      Scale      : 0.001 (mm → m)
      Bottom face: at Z = 0 in STL space

    MuJoCo mesh centroid offset (from console warning):
      X = -0.002361m
      Y = +0.000056m
      Z = +0.000747m
    → Applied as geom pos to shift mesh so body origin = bottom face center

    Coordinate convention: matches bottom_case.xml
      +X → keyboard length (left to right)
      +Y → keyboard width (front to back, rear = +Y)
      +Z → up

    Body origin: CENTER of bottom face of plate (Z=0 in body-local frame)
      In assembly, body pos z_world = top of EPDM foam
        EPDM foam top z_world = 0.003 + 0.0015 = 0.00450m
        Plate body pos z_world = 0.00450m  (bottom face sits on foam top)
        Plate center z_world   = 0.00450 + 0.00075 = 0.00525m
        Plate top z_world      = 0.00450 + 0.00150 = 0.00600m

    Assembly stack (no sound foam — dropped from BOM):
      Case floor top     : z_world = 0.003m
      EPDM foam (1.5mm)  : 0.003 → 0.00450m
      Aluminum plate (1.5mm): 0.00450 → 0.00600m
      Switches seat on plate top face at z_world = 0.00600m

    Switch cutout sites:
      84 sites at Cherry MX hole centers
      Standard MX grid: 19.05mm per U
      Grid centered on plate XY
      Site Z = plate top face = +0.0015m (body-local)

    Screw hole sites: 4 corner + 4 center (M3)
      Positions match bottom_case.xml screw boss XY

    Geometry:
      Visual + collision: mesh geom (Aluminum_Plate.stl)
        contype=0, conaffinity=0 — non-colliding (robot carries via teleport)
      Mesh file must be in models/meshes/ for station1.xml integration
  -->

